  "exact_numeric_statement": "For every natural k: ((k:Real)+12)^(k+11)<=3^12*12^11*6144^k*(k.factorial:Real).",
  "exact_composition_statement": "Under the sealed fixed-gap scalar hypotheses, let B=2*C*A, S=F+H0, D=2*B/rho. Then N(k+11,rho)<=(2*B*D^11*3^12*12^11)*S*(D*6144)^k*k! for every k. If Ebox>=0 and W(k)<=Ebox*N(k+11,rho) for every k, then W(k)<=Cstar*S*Astar^k*k!, with Cstar=2*B*Ebox*D^11*3^12*12^11 and Astar=D*6144. A pointwise norm-family version retains the same comparison for all x in a specified set.",
  "exact_scalar_hypotheses": [
    "0<rho<=1.",
    "C,A>=1; F,H0>=0.",
    "N_q(s)>=0 for every q and s in [0,rho].",
    "N_q(t)<=N_q(s) whenever 0<=s<=t<=rho.",
    "N_q(s)<=H0 for every q<=8 and s in [0,rho].",
    "The explicit unnormalized GrushinScalarFixedGapRecurrence N rho C A F."
  ],
  "numeric_proof": [
    "A single nonnegative term of the exponential series gives (k+12)^k/k!<=exp(k+12).",
    "The positive factorial denominator and exp(1)<3 imply (k+12)^k<=3^(k+12)*k!.",
    "The elementary induction k+1<=2^k gives k+12<=12*2^k.",
    "Split exponent k+11 and use (2^11)^k=2048^k and 3*2048=6144. No Stirling approximation or division by k is needed; k=0 is included."
  ],
  "composition_proof": [
    "Apply the exact sealed scalar fixed-gap result at r=k+11.",
    "Rewrite 2B*(r+1)/rho as D*(k+12). All multiplicative comparison coefficients are nonnegative.",
    "Apply the unconditional numeric theorem, then split D^(k+11) to obtain exactly the stated Cstar and Astar.",
    "Multiply by nonnegative Ebox only when a separate R24 comparison is explicitly supplied. No division by S or Ebox occurs."
  ],
